# UI Gotchas

- Menu primitives only work inside their menu context. Use Base UI menu primitives (`DropdownMenuItem`, `MenuPrimitive.Item`) only inside a `Menu.Root`/`DropdownMenu` wrapper. Prefer `onSelect` on VPK's `DropdownMenuItem`; it and `onClick` both close the menu, and `event.preventDefault()` keeps it open. For menu-item styling without menu context, use a plain `<button>` with Tailwind classes.
- Let the shared overlay primitive own both anchoring and surface chrome. For popups anchored to a trigger, use `Popover` from `components/ui/popover.tsx` with controlled `open`/`onOpenChange`; don't hardcode `position: fixed` pixel offsets or manual backdrop divs. For flyouts, popovers, dropdowns, and other overlay surfaces, do not add an outer border when overlay elevation/shadow already defines the surface (lint: the `shadcn/no-restyle` overlay contract rejects border/ring widths on `*Content` overlay surfaces) — the overlay background plus elevation alone avoids a double outline. Keep internal row separators only when they clarify grouped content.
- Hidden must mean unreachable, and visible must mean focusable with its focus ring intact. When animated or offscreen UI keeps interactive descendants mounted while visually hidden, pair the hidden state with both `aria-hidden` and `inert` on the wrapper, or unmount the controls, and add a focused closed-state regression test for the accessibility/focus contract. Hover-revealed actions on a visible surface are not closed UI: keep them in the tab order instead of using `hidden`/`display: none`, especially when descendant `:focus-visible` is the reveal trigger. Use an opacity/pointer-events treatment that becomes interactive on hover or keyboard focus, and add a regression that reaches the action by Tab without prior pointer hover. Anything focusable also needs outward focus-ring clearance from every clipping ancestor: VPK's widest shared treatment extends 4px, so scrollports should reserve that gutter with matching negative margin + padding when geometry must not move (full `-m-1 p-1`, or only the measured edge such as `-mt-1 pt-1`), and animated `0fr`/truncation wrappers should keep `overflow-hidden` at rest and switch to `has-[:focus-visible]:overflow-visible` after expansion. `z-index` only fixes overlap with siblings; never remove or shrink the ring, and do not replace a required scroll owner with `overflow: clip`.
- Global keyboard shortcuts, presenter controls, demo timers, and other window-level side effects must be gated by the active/open surface. Keyboard handlers must ignore events from focused controls (`input`, `textarea`, `select`, `button`, links, contenteditable, and activating ARIA roles), and timers must pause or remount while the surface is closed so hidden demos cannot advance in the background.
- Classify state by lifetime, and move draft state and persisted state in the same transition. Before hiding, unmounting, or re-keying a stateful surface, persist user-authored or committed state above temporary view switches and key it by stable entity identity; reset entity-local navigation when that identity changes. When an editor exposes multiple choices or destructive controls, Save must persist the selected choice, and delete/clear actions must also reset any local selection, draft, and open editor state so the next Save cannot silently recreate cleared data. Treat controlled collapse and rejected submissions as state transitions too: derive hidden action state from the current mode, and clear drafts only after confirmed success. Cover switch A → B → A, close/reopen, and rejected-submit paths, and add focused regression coverage for save/delete paths where accepted UI input can be discarded. Prove them by rendering the real surface with `renderComponent()`: type a draft, then close/reopen, `rerender` to entity B and back (add a `key` to model a host that re-keys), and assert what the viewer sees (examples: `components/blocks/agent-session/agent-session-link-work-item.behavior.test.js`, `components/blocks/jira-work-item/team-eu26/components/set-to-recur-popover.behavior.test.js`).
- Shared project components and cross-surface event handlers must not apply route/demo-specific labels, capabilities, copy, or intercept behavior to every consumer. Derive them from the payload or gate them with an explicit route, agent, or artifact discriminator, then add a focused non-target regression test.
- For composer directory autocomplete during async/debounced auto-tagging, separate visible suggestions from acceptable state. If the list stays visible while a query/range is stale, block Tab/Enter/Cmd-number/ghost acceptance until the state is recomputed, and add a focused regression for stale-range acceptance.
- For flex rows with truncating text, every flexible wrapper that must shrink needs `min-w-0`; fixed metadata, icons, and separators should be `shrink-0` so the intended text segment owns the ellipsis. Include a long-label fixture or regression assertion when adding hover-reveal actions beside truncating copy.
- When animated panels compute a fixed height before applying `overflow-hidden`, derive constants from the actual rendered geometry (slot size + padding + borders + dividers) instead of desired row names. Validate the measured row/panel height with a focused test or browser measurement so sticky footers and bottom gaps do not get clipped.
- For ADS Toggle parity work, lock geometry before token polish: use ADS content-box geometry, keep the regular thumb at 12px, and use `@atlaskit/icon/core/check-mark` + `@atlaskit/icon/core/cross` (`size="small"`) wrapped in VPK `Icon`.
- On pages that render multiple Sonner demos, give each `<Toaster />` a unique `id` (lint requires the `id`) and pass matching `toasterId` in `toast.*` calls so a single action does not render through multiple toasters.
